Tuesday
Interviews with Sano=E4=BC=9A=E9=95=B7 and DCM! It was awesome. Because we =
were in Wakayama
for DCM, we were able to go over to eat dinner at a Filipino member's
house. Her name (or at least what we call her is V=E5=A7=89=E5=A6=B9(V shim=
ai)) I ended up
sitting by their water cooler and V=E5=A7=89=E5=A6=B9 was laughing to tears=
 about how it
was a trap and now I have to get water for everyone when they need refills.
I was also laughing so much to the point of tears just because of how funny
she thought this simple thing was. It was a riot. She made a bunch of
different food, one thing was like crossections of pig leg or something;
the texture made it so hard to eat, I needed to chew it with something else
in my mouth (I didn't by the way lol). I only had a third then gave the
rest to my companion. Super sweet family. When we were back home in our
apartment that night a member showed up with food at our apartment at
almost midnight, it was nuts. He's not 100% with it I don't think, but he's
super kind to bring by food.

Wednesday we stopped by the art store lady again, this time we were able to
put some of our Eikaiwa flyers in her shop! She also sent me out of the
store with more art supplies but made me not pay for it =F0=9F=98=AD=F0=9F=
=98=AD she's
Impossible bro I literally wanna help out her store. She's so sweet, we
invited her to our Eikaiwa, gonna try and invite her to church next time we
meet. Also they are closed on Sundays so there's a good chance she can!!!
Tonight we tried out a game night instead of Eikaiwa, and everyone loved it
but Shiko lol. He can get over it though =F0=9F=98=82=F0=9F=98=82 We played=
 a bit of poker
together so hopefully that helped him enjoy it a bit lol. He really lives
Eikaiwa. It went pretty well in general, we are going to try it on the
first Wednesday of every month going forward.

Thursday
Today was awesome. We got to meet with Setsuko and her friend Asako to play
Ground Golf! Sister Dono agreed to join us for the lesson, but she really
just got roped into playing Ground Golf with us lol. I could tell she
wasn't maybe thrilled lol. afterwards though, she was able to talk a lot
about the Church with Setsuko. She also explained a bit of the role that
women play in God's work. It was brief, but really neat. Hopefully we can
have Asako more involved next chance we have a lesson. Before the Ground
Golf Magbago=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 and I went to Wendy's and actually got some =
food. Low-key
=E2=AC=87=EF=B8=8F=F0=9F=97=9D mega mid, way better in America. On the way =
home from Ground Golf, we
stopped by a member's house and left a note since they weren't there. Later
that day they actually called and said thanks! =F0=9F=99=8F Tonight was our=
 last
dinner outing with Jiro, he is going to Australia! We went to an Udon shop,
it was super tasty. Jiro asked us some weird questions in the car ride too
which was fun lol. Probably don't wanna write them in my email lol. We
figured out more of where he'll be in Australia so we can refer him better.
We exchanged contact info and sent him off with a hug.

Friday
We got up pretty early this morning to go all the way down to Gobo to
participate in an Eikaiwa at a high school?! It was crazy. We walked almost
2 hours from the station to the school, it was a long walk. We got there
and I felt like I was in an anime. It was weird to be in a Japanese school.
It was fun to talk with the students, but some of them were less than
enthusiastic lol. Looking forward to next month=E2=80=99s class (if I'm sti=
ll
around). I also met a guy at church fixing the Air conditioning, When I
asked him if he knew a Brother Killian, he said yeah, I do? And I told him
he's my uncle and his jaw just dropped lol. He also happened to see us when
we went to get Udon too lol. He=E2=80=99s super awesome =F0=9F=98=81

Saturday
We had our first Eikaiwa class in Ozaki! Unfortunately there were only a
few previous participants that showed up, and there weren't any kids that
came for the youth class =F0=9F=98=82 Before now we haven't exactly had man=
y chances
to get the word out so there's still hope =F0=9F=98=81 today we also got so=
me tasty
Okonomiyaki at a shop called Mugen (endless). It was gas.

On Sunday I gave my talk! It was fabulous. I thought it went well. Below is
what I read from and translated in Japanese. It's pretty basic but it was
tricky on the fly haha.

My talk

By Kaden Killian

(Explain how I always title my talks that)

Today I have been asked to talk missionary work

I have been a missionary for less than a year

Just like my introduction paper says, I have served in ibaraki, Marugame,
and now in Sennan.

I haven't been a missionary for very long, but I have already learned so
much. I believe that everyone of you guys can learn through missionary work
as well

I think that everyone can grow from a mission. There are new experiences,
you meet new people, and you even get to live with a lot of different
companions throughout your mission. I have learned so much from my past and
present companions.

Like I said, I think everyone probably will grow from a mission, but there
are a lot of things that we can do that will change how much we grow.

For me, I have found that I have learned and grown the most by turning
outside of myself, and looking to those around me. This could be friends,
ward members, and even my companions.

Basically, by turning outwards we are becoming more like the Savior, and we
are doing Missionary work.

I want to talk a little bit about what the meaning of missionary work is. I
think that missionary work is teaching others like the Savior would. This
of course can be about the gospel, but what else did Jesus Christ do
besides just teaching about the gospel?

Let's read some scriptures to find out.

3rd Nephi 11:9 he reached out
And it came to pass that he stretched forth his hand=E2=80=A6

3rd Nephi 17:7 he healed
=E2=80=A6Bring them hither and I will heal them, for I have compassion upon=
 you; my
bowels are filled with mercy.

Mark 8:6 he fed
6 And he commanded the people to sit down on the ground: and he took the
seven loaves, and gave thanks, and brake, and gave to his disciples to set
before them; and they did set them before the people

These are a few things that we can do to do missionary work. I would invite
each of you to try and see what other things that Jesus did in the
scriptures during your own studies.

I'd like to recount one of my experiences I had back in Marugame. One time
I was by the beach with my companion Elder Martinson; While we were over
there, we saw a lady picking up trash. I noticed some trash nearby, and
decided to go over and help her out. She was very happy, and we were able
to introduce ourselves. She gave us some treats, then went to find nearby
workers to give treats to as well!

She reached out, she fed, and she healed (with treats).

This lady set a good example for me and my companion. She did not know us,
or the workers, and she was in a place that she did not know. I think that
we are the same way.

In my mission, as I have followed the example of this lady and the example
of the Savior, I have seen miracles and success. As we prioritize knowing
and interacting with those around us, we are following the example of the
Savior. We can find comfort and reassurance as we follow God=E2=80=99s plan=
 for us.

I believe that Jesus is our Savior. I have really felt his love. I have
also felt love from Heavenly father. I love you all, and I want to follow
Christ's example. I believe that even though I am imperfect, I can feel
peace as I try my best to be a good missionary.

I say these things in the name of Jesus Christ, Amen.

Also gonna wrap up my email here. Hope you guys are all doing well, I love
hearing from you all so don't hesitate to send me an email or 3 or 4 =F0=9F=
=98=89=F0=9F=98=82
Love you guys!!! Things are going better lately, increased efforts and
humility make all the difference.

Elder Killian

